 "idea_credit": "jacksonxly (r/LangChain): low-water-mark/IFC framing + staked/decaying standing. Roots: Biba 1977, Myers&Liskov DLM, CaMeL (2503.18813), Douceur Sybil 2002.",
 "verdict": "The security question is NOT the low-water-mark. Because poison and rare-true share one integrity distribution, the graded low-water-mark frontier is diagonal BY CONSTRUCTION (gap 0.03=noise~0): it trades security for utility ~1:1 and does not detect poison. The lever is the ORTHOGONAL earned-standing declassifier: it refunds ONLY the true items that already hold standing (in the toy, the 0.20≈P_AGED we set) of the lost true-recall (poison has no standing), but is bounded by COLD START (only ~34% of rare-true have standing; the rest = the irreducible tail Sybil-resistance can't refund) and defeated by SLEEPERS (standing is intent-blind), and it sits above a Sybil FLOOR (~0.95 forged-corroboration hijack) that no tau removes without destroying benign utility. So: RBAC gates the actor, IFC gates the data, membership-cost gates the identity — and the cold-start tail is the measured price of doing the last one without a trusted registrar."
}